  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-02T04:20:53.425Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Given an avatar with only a gestures playable layer and nothing else, the gestures layer will not animate non-humanoid bones (it's as if they've been masked out). A workaround is to create a dummy FX playable layer controller that has a single state with no motion. This is new behavior after the recent updates.\nHow to reproduce:\n1. Create a new unity project and extract this unity package: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1kWiRA97ffHKZckgsWgY6p8XadspVRu_I/view?usp=sharing\n2. Build the avatar named \"Bugged Avatar\" in \"Avatar Scene\". The wings do not animate\n3. Add the \"Dummy Controller\" to the FX Playable layer for the avatar.\n4. Build again. The wings now animate.\nThere was discussion on this in the VR Chat Discord on November 1st.",
